{"step_index":3473,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T18:31:08Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T21:31:08+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T21:31:09+03:00\nFile Path: `file:///d:/AI_Engineer/MSEMAX/README.md`\nTotal Lines: 424\nTotal Bytes: 15342\nShowing lines 1 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: <div align=\"center\">\n2: \n3: # MSEMAX\n4: \n5: **High-Performance OpenAI-Compatible API Gateway**\n6: \n7: [![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.12+-3776AB?style=flat-square&logo=python&logoColor=white)](https://python.org)\n8: [![FastAPI](https://img.shields.io/badge/FastAPI-0.111-009688?style=flat-square&logo=fastapi&logoColor=white)](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com)\n9: [![Docker](https://img.shields.io/badge/Docker-Ready-2496ED?style=flat-square&logo=docker&logoColor=white)](https://docker.com)\n10: [![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg?style=flat-square)](LICENSE)\n11: [![GitHub stars](https://img.shields.io/github/stars/MohamedElsayed-debug/MSEMAX?style=flat-square&logo=github)](https://github.com/MohamedElsayed-debug/MSEMAX/stargazers)\n12: \n13: A lightweight, production-ready API gateway that provides an OpenAI-compatible interface\n14: <br>\n15: for AI chat completions. Built with FastAPI for maximum async performance.\n16: \n17: <br>\n18: \n19: ### ❤️ Supporters\n20: \n21: [**Kareem Adel**](https://www.facebook.com/Kareemadel.official.account) — Owner & CEO at Wzila\n22: \n23: _(Want to see your name here? Check out the [Support This Project](#support-this-project) section!)_\n24: \n25: <br>\n26: \n27: [Features](#features) · [Quick Start](#quick-start) · [API Reference](#api-reference) · [Configuration](#configuration) · [Deployment](#deployment) · [Architecture](#architecture)\n28: \n29: </div>\n30: \n31: ---\n32: \n33: ## Features\n34: \n35: - **OpenAI-Compatible API** — Drop-in replacement for any OpenAI SDK, LangChain, n8n, or custom client. Supports both streaming (SSE) and non-streaming JSON responses.\n36: - **Async Architecture** — Non-blocking I/O with `asyncio` — handles concurrent connections on a single worker. No thread pool overhead.\n37: - **Response Sanitization** — Streaming-safe cleaner strips metadata noise, citations, entity tags, image groups, and product listings from AI responses in real-time.\n38: - **Rate Limiting & Concurrency Control** — Per-IP rate limiting via `slowapi` + global concurrency semaphore prevents upstream overload. Returns 429 immediately when at capacity.\n39: - **Proof-of-Work Solver** — Offloads CPU-intensive SHA3-512 PoW challenges to a `ProcessPoolExecutor` — bypasses the GIL using real CPU cores.\n40: - **Docker Ready** — One-command deployment with `docker compose`. Session data mounted as a volume for easy updates.\n41: \n42: **Additional features:** Smart session caching (mtime-based invalidation) · Bearer token authentication · Browser TLS fingerprint impersonation via `curl_cffi` · Built-in stress testing tool\n43: \n44: ---\n45: \n46: ## Quick Start\n47: \n48: ### Prerequisites\n49: \n50: | Requirement | Version | Purpose                               |\n51: | ----------- | ------- | ------------------------------------- |\n52: | Python      | 3.12+   | Runtime                               |\n53: | pip         | Latest  | Package manager                       |\n54: | Chromium    | Any     | Session capture only (via Playwright) |\n55: \n56: ### 1. Clone & Install\n57: \n58: ```bash\n59: git clone https://github.com/MohamedElsayed-debug/MSEMAX.git\n60: cd MSEMAX\n61: python -m venv venv\n62: source venv/bin/activate    # Linux/Mac\n63: # venv\\Scripts\\activate     # Windows\n64: pip install -r requirements.txt\n65: ```\n66: \n67: ### 2. Configure Environment\n68: \n69: ```bash\n70: cp .env.example .env\n71: nano .env  # Set MSE_MAX_KEY to a secure random string\n72: ```\n73: \n74: ### 3. Capture Session\n75: \n76: ```bash\n77: python get_session.py\n78: ```\n79: \n80: > **Important** — This step opens a browser window. You must:\n81: >\n82: > 1. Log in to your ChatGPT account (if not already)\n83: > 2. Send **any** short message in the chat (only if the script doesn't capture everything automatically within a few seconds)\n84: > 3. Wait for the script to confirm all tokens are captured\n85: >\n86: > The captured data is saved to `session_data.json`. You only need to do this once (until the session expires).\n87: \n88: ### 4. Start the Server\n89: \n90: ```bash\n91: python app.py\n92: ```\n93: \n94: The API is now running at `http://localhost:8000`.\n95: \n96: ### 5. Verify\n97: \n98: ```bash\n99: curl http://localhost:8000/health\n100: ```\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
